00:21:42.970 --> 00:21:44.650
PLOUT: Coming
together this morning

00:21:44.650 --> 00:21:49.780
to warm each other's souls, to
inspire one another to continue

00:21:49.780 --> 00:21:54.100
the struggle for
equality, let us listen to

00:21:54.100 --> 00:21:56.770
and let us act upon
the commandments found

00:21:56.770 --> 00:21:59.170
in the Bible.

00:21:59.170 --> 00:22:04.120
In the Book of Exodus, God
calls upon each one of us

00:22:04.120 --> 00:22:08.200
to teach our sons and
daughters, to teach them

00:22:08.200 --> 00:22:12.310
the story of the exodus
from Egypt, the liberation

00:22:12.310 --> 00:22:15.130
from the house of bondage.

00:22:15.130 --> 00:22:17.680
This duty of
teaching our children

00:22:17.680 --> 00:22:22.900
diligently is repeated in
the Book of Deuteronomy.

00:22:22.900 --> 00:22:27.160
There, we are commanded to
love God with all of our mind,

00:22:27.160 --> 00:22:30.890
with all of our strength,
and with all of our being,

00:22:30.890 --> 00:22:35.710
to set these sacred words which
are commanded upon our hearts,

00:22:35.710 --> 00:22:39.430
to teach them faithfully
to our children,

00:22:39.430 --> 00:22:44.050
to speak of them in our home
and on our way when we lie down

00:22:44.050 --> 00:22:46.240
and when we rise up.

00:22:46.240 --> 00:22:50.500
And we should bind them
as a sign upon our hand

00:22:50.500 --> 00:22:53.470
and let them be a
symbol before our eyes,

00:22:53.470 --> 00:22:57.120
inscribing them on the
door posts of our house

00:22:57.120 --> 00:22:59.620
and on our gates.

00:22:59.620 --> 00:23:03.040
Scripture commands us that
teaching and learning,

00:23:03.040 --> 00:23:09.370
the vehicles of education, are
not a privilege, but a duty.

00:23:09.370 --> 00:23:14.020
Learning and teaching are
active states of being.

00:23:14.020 --> 00:23:17.590
Day and night, let us labor to
bring the fruits of education

00:23:17.590 --> 00:23:21.430
to every person, to
erase the inequalities

00:23:21.430 --> 00:23:26.220
in educational opportunity
which so afflict our society,

00:23:26.220 --> 00:23:28.570
and let us search for
and then reach out

00:23:28.570 --> 00:23:33.220
to help those who are at a
disadvantage to empower them

00:23:33.220 --> 00:23:37.120
with all of the knowledge and
wisdom, the skills and learning

00:23:37.120 --> 00:23:41.710
experiences that will be the key
that opens the door to a better

00:23:41.710 --> 00:23:44.980
and more just life.

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:46.720
On this morning,
we gather to honor

00:23:46.720 --> 00:23:51.160
the spirit of Martin Luther
King, Jr, a blessed memory,

00:23:51.160 --> 00:23:56.470
to carry on and transmit the
legacy he has bequeathed.

00:23:56.470 --> 00:24:01.750
As we now carry his torch
and this generation,

00:24:01.750 --> 00:24:04.930
let us keep in mind that
every generation that

00:24:04.930 --> 00:24:08.440
inherits the
victories of the past

00:24:08.440 --> 00:24:12.880
will not enjoy them unless
it strives to understand,

00:24:12.880 --> 00:24:16.180
appreciate, and cherish them
as though they themselves

00:24:16.180 --> 00:24:18.340
have fought for them.

00:24:18.340 --> 00:24:23.290
Each generation must
discover freedom anew.

00:24:23.290 --> 00:24:28.030
Each must ever earn
its claim to liberty.

00:24:28.030 --> 00:24:31.250
Let us therefore
each ask of ourselves

00:24:31.250 --> 00:24:36.850
how we intend, as individuals,
to bring equal educational

00:24:36.850 --> 00:24:40.750
and work opportunity
to those in need,

00:24:40.750 --> 00:24:47.620
how we intend in our own way to
carry the torch of yesteryear.

00:24:47.620 --> 00:24:51.430
Looking back in time, I think
of my late father, Walter Plout,

00:24:51.430 --> 00:24:56.080
a rabbi who was a
Freedom Rider in 1962

00:24:56.080 --> 00:24:59.380
fighting the battle to
desegregate public facilities

00:24:59.380 --> 00:25:02.620
in Georgia and Florida.

00:25:02.620 --> 00:25:06.690
His heartfelt
responsibility is now mine,

00:25:06.690 --> 00:25:08.980
and I, like the rest
of us in this room,

00:25:08.980 --> 00:25:13.360
have a responsibility to
face the unique challenges

00:25:13.360 --> 00:25:17.470
of inequality in
our own generation,

00:25:17.470 --> 00:25:21.850
continuing the work of
those who came before us.

00:25:21.850 --> 00:25:25.780
As we sit and break
bread together and listen

00:25:25.780 --> 00:25:29.530
and discuss on this great
morning of celebration

00:25:29.530 --> 00:25:33.400
of the life and the spirit
of Martin Luther King, Jr,

00:25:33.400 --> 00:25:38.920
let us be grateful for
this wonderful opportunity

00:25:38.920 --> 00:25:43.360
of a community coming together,
striving to forever renew

00:25:43.360 --> 00:25:45.940
a shared vision.

00:25:45.940 --> 00:25:48.040
Let us remember
that after all, we

00:25:48.040 --> 00:25:51.610
are here at this great
Institute of research,

00:25:51.610 --> 00:25:55.480
learning, and teaching
because we accept our mission

00:25:55.480 --> 00:26:01.420
to be proactive in fulfilling
the dream of providing teaching

00:26:01.420 --> 00:26:06.770
and learning experiences
for every American in need.

00:26:06.770 --> 00:26:09.010
And while a good meal
now awaits us all,

00:26:09.010 --> 00:26:11.850
there is much more
to anticipate.

00:26:11.850 --> 00:26:15.670
A 2000-year-old Jewish
saying from the Talmud

00:26:15.670 --> 00:26:20.500
